# Default Gateway

A **default gateway** is normally the router interface connected to the
same local network as a host.

For example:

``` text
PC IP:       192.168.2.2
Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0
Gateway:     192.168.2.1
```

If the PC wants to communicate with a device outside its local network,
it sends the traffic to the default gateway.

Example:

``` text
PC
 |
 | Destination is outside local network
 v
Default Gateway / Router
 |
 v
Other Network
```

The default gateway is therefore very important for communication
between different networks.

