# Day 14 Summary

Today I learned how routers are used to connect different networks, how
routing tables help routers choose paths, and how LANs can be designed
as one or multiple local networks.

The two Packet Tracer activities helped me understand these concepts
practically. The most useful part was using Simulation Mode to inspect
ARP requests, broadcast frames, MAC addresses, IP addresses, and the
movement of PDUs through the network.

**Main takeaway:**

> IP tells the network where the packet needs to go, while MAC addresses
> help deliver the frame on the current local network. ARP helps
> discover the required MAC address, and routers are responsible for
> moving traffic between different IP networks.

